{"id":"neet-2026r-q059","pn":59,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"Solutions","st":"Deviation from Raoult's law","q":"Consider the following statements about the solutions formed by mixing two liquids.\nA. An ideal solution thus formed obeys Raoult’s law throughout the composition range.\nB. Mixture of chloroform and acetone shows negative deviation from Raoult’s law.\nC. Mixture of aniline and phenol shows positive deviation from Raoult’s law.","o":["B and C only","A only","A and C only","A and B only"],"c":3,"s":"In phenol and aniline, the hydrogen bond between the phenolic proton and the lone pair on the nitrogen of aniline is stronger than the hydrogen bonds between similar molecules.\nSo the mixture shows negative deviation, not positive. Statement C is wrong.\nStatements A and B are correct."},
{"id":"neet-2026-q076","pn":76,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Solutions","st":"Concentration terms and Henry's law","q":"Identify the correct statements :\n(A) The molality of 2.5 g of ethanoic acid (Molar mass : 60 g mol⁻¹) in 75 g of benzene solution is 0.556 m.\n(B) The molarity of a solution containing 5 g of NaOH (molar mass : 40 g mol⁻¹) in 450 mL of solution is 0.278 M at 298 K.\n(C) Aquatic species are more comfortable in cold water.\n(D) The solubility of gas increases with decrease in pressure.\n(E) For a binary mixture of A and B, the number of moles of A and B are nA and nB respectively. The mole fraction of B will be x_B = nA/(nA × nB).\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :","o":["A and C only","A, B and C only","A, D and E only","A and B only"],"c":1,"s":"(A) Molality = (2.5 × 1000)/(60 × 75) = 0.556 molal. Correct.\n(B) Molarity = (5 × 1000)/(40 × 450) = 0.278 M. Correct.\n(C) Henry's constant K_H increases with temperature, so gas solubility falls as temperature rises. Cold water holds more dissolved oxygen, so aquatic species are more comfortable in it. Correct.\n(D) By Henry's law p = K_H x, so solubility increases when pressure increases. Statement D is incorrect.\n(E) x_B = nB/(nA + nB), not nA/(nA + nB). Statement E is incorrect.\nSo A, B and C are correct."},
{"id":"neet-2026-q077","pn":77,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Solutions","st":"Non-ideal solutions, Raoult's law","q":"Mixture of chloroform and acetone forms a solution with negative deviation from Raoult's law due to :","o":["Formation of hydrogen bonding between acetone and chloroform","Increase in escaping tendency of molecules of each component.","Stronger intermolecular forces between chloroform molecules than those between chloroform and acetone molecules.","Repulsive forces."],"c":0,"s":"Acetone and chloroform show negative deviation from Raoult's law because of stronger H-bonding between the two in the mixture.\nThe H-bond is formed between the C=O oxygen of acetone and the H of chloroform (C=O ----- H–CCl₃).\nSo the escaping tendency decreases.\nTherefore the vapour pressure decreases and the boiling point increases.","sfig":{"w":300,"h":96,"alt":"Acetone (CH3 and H3C on a C double bonded to O) with a dashed line from its O to the H of chloroform, H–C bonded to three Cl.","d":[["t",10,14,"Acetone",""],["t",200,14,"Chloroform",""],["t",26,42,"CH₃","m"],["t",26,84,"H₃C","m"],["t",66,62,"C","m"],["l",40,40,58,52,""],["l",40,76,58,64,""],["l",74,60,88,60,""],["l",74,56,88,56,""],["t",97,62,"O","m"],["l",106,58,160,58,"d"],["t",168,62,"H","m"],["l",176,58,190,58,""],["t",198,62,"C","m"],["l",206,52,220,40,""],["l",206,58,222,58,""],["l",206,64,220,76,""],["t",232,40,"Cl","m"],["t",232,62,"Cl","m"],["t",232,84,"Cl","m"]]}},
{"id":"neet-2026r-q080","pn":80,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"Solutions","st":"Ideal solutions","q":"Assertion A: For an ideal solution formed by mixing liquids P and Q, ΔmixH = 0 and ΔmixV = 0\nReason R: No interactions occur between P and Q\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.","o":["Both A and R are correct but R is NOT the correct explanation of A","A is correct but R is not correct","A is not correct but R is correct","Both A and R are correct and R is the correct explanation of A"],"c":1,"s":"For an ideal solution, ΔmixH = 0 and ΔmixV = 0, so A is correct.\nThe energy needed to break P–P and Q–Q interactions equals the energy released on forming P–Q interactions.\nSo interactions do occur between P and Q, and R is not correct."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q066","pn":66,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Solutions","st":"Types of solutions","q":"Match List-I with List-II\nList-I (Example) → List-II (Type of Solution)\nA. Humidity — I. Solid in solid\nB. Alloys — II. Liquid in gas\nC. Amalgams — III. Solid in gas\nD. Smoke — IV. Liquid in solid\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:","o":["A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III","A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III","A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV"],"c":1,"s":"Humidity is a solution of liquid in gas.\nAlloy is a solution of solid in solid.\nAmalgam is a solution of liquid in solid.\nSmoke is a solution of solid in gas."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q079","pn":79,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Solutions","st":"Elevation of boiling point","q":"Which of the following aqueous solution will exhibit highest boiling point?","o":["0.01M Urea","0.01M KNO₃","0.01M Na₂SO₄","0.015M C₆H₁₂O₆"],"c":2,"s":"ΔT_b = i K_b × m\nΔT_b ∝ i × m\nTake molarity as same as molality.\n(1) 0.01M Urea: i × m = 1 × 0.01 = 0.01\n(2) 0.01M KNO₃: i × m = 2 × 0.01 = 0.02\n(3) 0.01M Na₂SO₄: i × m = 3 × 0.01 = 0.03\n(4) 0.015M C₆H₁₂O₆: i × m = 1 × 0.015 = 0.015\nT_b' = T_b* + ΔT_b\nHigher the value of (i × m), higher is the boiling point."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q081","pn":81,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Solutions","st":"Raoult's law deviations","q":"5 moles of liquid X and 10 moles of liquid Y make a solution having a vapour pressure of 70 torr. The vapour pressures of pure X and Y are 63 torr and 78 torr respectively. Which of the following is true regarding the described solution?","o":["The solution shows positive deviation.","The solution shows negative deviation.","The solution is ideal.","The solution has volume greater than the sum of individual volumes."],"c":1,"s":"P_total = X_x P°_x + X_y P°_y\n= (5/15) × 63 + (10/15) × 78\n= 21 + 52\n= 73 torr\nObserved total pressure of the solution is 70 torr.\nIt is less than the calculated total pressure.\nHence, it shows negative deviation."}
